KEPT.poke(same(p: l)) keeps a view of the frame slot 'l' (claimed at line 15) in the global 'KEPT', which every routine reaches, and the build can't compare those later uses with where that view's place is given back: keep a Stamped of the entity there (its stamp(), read back with fetch(), which fails once the entity has ended), make the field an &E? when one holder keeps the value, or hand the view as an argument to the routines that use it. An Addr (the view's .to[Addr](), turned back with .to[@T?]() and a when) is for links the program keeps right itself, such as a runtime's queues
